^L


The problem with quaffing from a sink instead of kicking it (in order to get 
a ring) is that with quaffing there is a chance that the sink will become a
fountain--'the pipes burst...'  Beyond that, water elementals and puddings 
seem equally nasty.  If one is powerful enough to take on either one, go
for puddings.  (And, potentially, succubi.) 

In terms of prices, I don't remember offhand what the price of most rings
for most average characters w/ average charisma are but they range from 
150-300 zorkmids.  The 400 zorkmid rings--ie. the most expensive you will
find--are regeneration and polymorph control.  They are well worth it though.  
Expect to pay 533 zorkmids if you are ugly.  



